"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7Sbq23","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Most of the changes look pretty trivial. In particular, the `RequiredParam` changes mostly verify themselves, due to the protections of the class :)\n\nI'm a bit more reserved about the `RequiredResult` changes. There is no way of making absolutely certain that a function doesn't introduce a non-erroneous `nullptr` return path in the future. Having it marked as `RequiredResult` may be incompatible with projects that assume `nullptr` is an error.\nI have no ideas to avoid this, but since `nullptr` _does_ mean some kind of error for many getter functions maybe we don't _need_ to address this either?\n\nThe only other caveat i have is that in its current state, `RequiredParam` is slightly slower than `const Ref &`, since it requires a copy of the `Ref` be made. This overhead is hopefully not relevant in any of the functions, but I can't say for sure.\n(I have a plan to optimize this in the future, so the regression should hopefully be temporary anyway)","state":"C